  "mathematical_reasons": [
    "The sealed theorem retains C2 potential, both global Hessian bounds, positive alpha<=beta, eta>0 and beta*eta<=1. Its only structural extension is finite real Hilbert/Borel E including rank0. There is no extra probability, density, derivative, Lp, core, normalization, law, domain or closure certificate among the binders.",
    "MacroscopicEnergy is used for actual Gibbs mu and actual outer nu probability, the EVERY-y kernel equality hSd and genuine Tf/gradientTf MemLp witnesses. It derives exponential L1 from positive Gibbs partition, genuine augmentation and Markov conditional R/S, bounded compact-observer mean, and gradient-square integrability dominated by the integrable conditional variance with a finite positive-denominator coefficient. These are produced internally under the same source hypotheses.",
    "The exact SAME mu/J/nu are local definitional aliases of the independent Gaussian augmentation and its second marginal. S is the literal normalized source-volume tilt with inverse half and coefficient1/(8eta). funext of hSd proves equality of the entire mean functions. That equality rewrites both the actual mean and its actual gradient in MemLp; this is not differentiation of an AE representative.",
    "GaussianMarginalGradient constructs one G before f is introduced. Its internally produced positive C2 Gaussian density rho=C*Z has true L1 and mass1; W=-log rho yields the actual normalized tilted law. WeightedGradient constructs exactly the compact-smooth gradient graph, derives density via smooth L2 approximation and closability by compact vector-field weighted integration by parts and dense test orthogonality. G is not joint blockD or a caller-supplied core.",
    "LiteralReflectedMean yields global whole-function C1 for the identical literal S mean. Its Gibbs integrability, literal tilted composition and normalized affine reflection, including inverse half and factor8eta, are internal. Parent GaussianReflectedMean supplies dominated differentiation and derivative continuity; the successful source mean is differentiable everywhere, so gradient cannot be the default fderiv-zero artifact.",
    "WeightedC1GradientDomain consumes this same G, its exact graph characterization, closability, C1Tf and both genuine L2 witnesses. Smooth radial cutoffs exhaust space with chi_n->1 and derivative bound C/(n+1). Dominated squared L2 convergence controls function and gradient, with the extra Tf*gradient(chi_n) term tending to0. Compact C1 cutoffs are jointly mollified in function and gradient, then a closed graph limit gives the canonical pair. No Tf compactness, spatial moment, global score bound or higher smoothness is assumed.",
    "The Test PUP consumer uses the actual reflected joint-L2 isometry U, conditional projection P, real g=f(snd), Pg=g and the actual Ag source-mean representative. EVERY-y hSd transports that representative to the SAME literal Tf used in G.closure.graph. This is a genuine joint operator/outer-law consumer; it does not claim a full rough operator extension.",
    "In dimension0, V=0 with alpha=beta=eta=1 satisfies the original curvature/step conditions because all direction vectors are0. The noncentered observer1 is genuinely smooth and compact on the singleton. Actual source mean=1 and whole gradient=0 are transferred into the canonical same-nu Lp pair using MemLp.toLp_congr; neither centering nor an all-zero input is substituted.",
    "All four public production parents are actual calls and all new body ingredients are consumed: mu/nu probability installs the required finite-measure instances; G density/closability/closedness/graph are returned; source equality, L2 witnesses and C1 feed the existing adapter. Wider siblings returned by MacroscopicEnergy are deliberately unused consequences, not new hypotheses or fake extra progress. No duplicate private provider, new instance or wrapper-only theorem is introduced."
